cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "bend-spike: configuration-independent verification of a machine-protection interlock chain (JET case study) in Bend 2"
abstract: >-
  A verified reference model of the JET wall-protection chain (JTT / RTPS / PTN / DMS)
  written in Bend 2: laws over every urgency order, control state, event and counter value,
  decided by a finite certificate and lifted to universal theorems by reflection, with
  soundness lemmas for the specification predicates, an independent Python re-execution,
  an adversarial mutation bank (73 defects) judged against specification constants, and
  differential testing of a production implementation. The code and the documentation were
  produced by a human author working with an AI assistant (Claude); the adversarial reviews
  recorded in the docs are automated passes, not independent human evaluation.
authors:
